+- Outgoing commits are audited, not only the current working tree. A secret added in an older outgoing commit and deleted later is still blocked. Outgoing merge commits require manual review. Incoming commits are also audited before controlled pulls; workflow mutations, secrets, symlinks, submodules, merge commits, and paths outside the source allowlist block automatic deployment.
 - Review authorization is HMAC-signed, bound to the active Superadmin session, exact repository/branch/action/push mode, reviewed HEAD/remote SHA, file count and content/mode manifest, and expires within 10 minutes.
 - For pushes, `npm test` and `npm run build` must both pass before authorization is issued.
 - After staging, Git blob IDs and modes are rechecked against the reviewed manifest. The push uses the exact reviewed/generated commit SHA rather than a moving `HEAD`. A concurrent remote change is rejected by normal non-force Git push semantics.
+- Managed-workspace mode verifies project identity (`package.json` name plus required 67 source anchors) before mirroring deployment files, preventing an unrelated repository from being bound to `/67`. The managed workspace lives outside the deployment tree and never runs `git init` inside `/67`.
+- Managed pulls use an affected-file backup and atomic replacement for approved source files; failures attempt rollback of touched deployment files. Runtime/secrets remain outside the Git mirror.
 
